Launcher layer -> spacebar simlayer with f Finder, s Safari, t Terminal, c Chrome
Home/end text nav -> Cmd+h to home and Cmd+l to end only if requested
App-specific -> use existing app condition names if present

Goku syntax reminders:
[:a :b] means a maps to b
[:!Ca :b] means Cmd+a maps to b
[:!Oa :b] means Opt+a maps to b
[:!Ta :b] means Ctrl+a maps to b
[:!Sa :b] means Shift+a maps to b
! means mandatory modifier: C Cmd, O Opt, T Ctrl, S Shift, F Fn
# means optional modifier
"##" means any optional modifier
Shell action format: [:key ["absolute command here"]]
Condition format: [:a :b [:app "Terminal"]]
Variable layer pattern: [:##caps_lock ["nav-mode" 1] nil {:afterup ["nav-mode" 0]}], then rules with ["nav-mode" 1]
Simlayer pattern: :simlayers {:nav-mode {:key :d}}, then {:simlayer :nav-mode :rules [...]}

